This repository builds on, and its builds incorporate, the following projects:

- Suwayomi-Server (https://github.com/Suwayomi/Suwayomi-Server), MPL-2.0. Included as the git
  submodule extension-host/vendor/suwayomi (unmodified). Files under extension-host/*/src/overlay that
  replace Suwayomi files are modified copies and remain MPL-2.0 (see their headers).
- Android API signature (AOSP frameworks/base, tag android-11.0.0_r1), Apache-2.0. Vendored in
  extension-host/android-stubs/api (see NOTICE and METADATA there); the stub jar is generated from it.
- dex2jar (https://github.com/ThexXTURBOXx/dex2jar), Apache-2.0. One file is patched as an overlay
  (extension-host/source-api/src/overlay/java/com/googlecode/dex2jar/ir/ts/NewTransformer.java).
- AOSP android.graphics.ColorMatrix, Apache-2.0 (extension-host/android-compat overlay).
- Eclipse OpenJ9 and Eclipse OMR (https://github.com/eclipse-openj9), used under Apache-2.0; and the
  OpenJDK class library and native libraries from openj9-openjdk-jdk21, GPL-2.0 with the Classpath
  Exception. jvm-ios fetches their sources at pinned commits; the patches applied to them are in
  jvm-ios/patches and are licensed like the files they modify.
- Library dependencies of the extension host resolved by Gradle (see extension-host/gradle and
  the version catalogs), each under its own licence.

The complete licence texts and notices for everything the Oneechan app ships are generated by the
app repository's licence tooling and shown in the app (More > About > Open-source licenses).

Source code
-----------
This repository holds the source code of the open-source components that the Oneechan app distributes
under licences that require it to be available: the OpenJDK class library and its native libraries
(GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception), Eclipse OpenJ9 and Eclipse OMR, and the MPL-2.0 and EPL-2.0
components. That includes Oneechan's modifications (extension-host overlays, jvm-ios/patches) and the
scripts used to build them. Each version of the app is built from a fixed commit of this repository
(its submodule commit); upstream sources are at the URLs listed per component in the app's
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Written offer: for at least three years after a version of the app was last distributed, anyone may
obtain the complete corresponding source code of these components for that version, on request, at no
more than the cost of physically performing the distribution. To request it, open an issue at
https://github.com/leros1337/oneechan-runtime/issues.

Unmodified MPL-2.0 and EPL-2.0 components (for example Rhino and logback) are also available from
their upstream URL at the exact version listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
